<?xml version="1.0"?>
<!--
  nav_test_line.xml - ONE planned leg to the team's approach point, for testing
  obstacle avoidance on its own.

  The sim test is a LiDAR-only object (a platform) sitting on the straight line to
  a goal: send the goal with the approach lat/lon as the destination and watch the
  boat plan round it.

      ros2 action send_goal /crsd/safe_passage crusader_msgs/action/SafePassage \
        "{tier: 0, timeout_s: 300, approach_latitude: 1.2806, approach_longitude: 103.8560594}"

  Nothing else is in the tree on purpose: no perception, no confirmation handshake,
  no orbit, so whatever the boat does is the planned leg. NavigateTo plans around
  every known object, holds when it cannot, and FAILS after 15 s blocked, which
  fails the tree and ends the mission with a clear result (NO_ENTRY). The mission
  timeout and cancel live in bt_runner_node, not here. Run it with bt_runner's
  nav_mode on (or shadow, to see the plan drawn and the legacy leg driven).

  The IsAutonomous guard band is still here: even a test must stop when the pilot
  takes the mode away.
-->
<root BTCPP_format="4" main_tree_to_execute="NavTestLine">
  <BehaviorTree ID="NavTestLine">
    <ReactiveSequence name="guard_band">

      <IsAutonomous/>

      <NavigateTo target="approach" tolerance="2.0"/>

    </ReactiveSequence>
  </BehaviorTree>
</root>
